---
layout: base.njk
title: whoami
section: about
description: Operator record, hardware inventory and contact channels.
---
{% from "macros.njk" import rule %}

<!-- ══ IDENTITY ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<header class="mb-16 pt-4">
  <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-sm text-ink-dim">
    <span class="text-signal">$</span> whoami &amp;&amp; finger {{ site.author }}
  </p>
  <h1 class="title-card text-[clamp(2.5rem,9vw,5.5rem)] leading-[0.92]">{{ site.author }}</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-dim">{{ site.role }}</p>
</header>

<section class="mb-20 grid items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-6" data-reveal>

  <!-- passwd entry -->
  <div class="panel md:col-span-4">
    <div class="panel-hd">
      <span><span class="text-signal/50" aria-hidden="true">▚▚</span> /etc/passwd</span>
      <span class="text-signal/50">read-only</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body">
      <dl class="font-mono text-sm">
        {% set fields = [
          { k: "login",  v: site.author },
          { k: "uid",    v: "1000" },
          { k: "shell",  v: "/bin/zsh" },
          { k: "home",   v: "/home/" + site.author },
          { k: "gecos",  v: site.role }
        ] %}
        {% for f in fields %}
          <div class="flex gap-4 border-b border-line/60 py-2 last:border-b-0">
            <dt class="w-20 shrink-0 text-ink-faint">{{ f.k }}</dt>
            <dd class="text-ink-hi">{{ f.v }}</dd>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Avatar plate -->
  <div class="panel bracketed group md:col-span-2">
    <div class="panel-hd">
      <span><span class="text-signal/50" aria-hidden="true">▚▚</span> avatar</span>
      <span class="text-signal/50">1-bit</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pool flex aspect-square items-center justify-center bg-bg-deep/50">
      <span class="title-card text-[7rem] leading-none" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ site.author | first | upper }}
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="border-t border-line px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">
      <span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-ok align-middle animate-bar-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      logged in — tty1
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ BIO ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="mb-20" data-reveal>
  {{ rule("readme", "~/README.md") }}
  <div class="max-w-measure space-y-5 font-mono text-sm leading-[1.85] text-ink">
    <p>
      I build software, mostly close to the metal and mostly on my own machines.
      Lately that means inference servers on Apple Silicon, an iOS keyboard that
      talks to whichever model you point it at, and agents that have to cite their
      sources. The through-line is latency and control — things that run locally,
      with your own keys, and answer fast.
    </p>
    <p>
      I like problems where the constraint is real: a keyboard extension that cannot
      touch the microphone, a GPU budget that will not grow, a model that has to load
      before anyone loses patience. Working inside a hard limit produces better designs
      than working without one.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is the long-form record — notes from the field, whatever I'm building
      that week, and the occasional post that outgrew a note. No analytics, no
      newsletter, no popups. Just files on a server.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ HARDWARE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="mb-20" data-reveal>
  {{ rule("lshw", "inventory") }}

  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {% set kit = [
      { label: "languages", items: ["C++", "Swift", "TypeScript", "Python", "SQL"] },
      { label: "stack", items: ["MLX", "Metal", "SwiftUI", "Node", "Cloudflare"] },
      { label: "bench", items: ["Xcode", "CMake", "Neovim", "tmux", "Git"] }
    ] %}
    {% for group in kit %}
      <div class="group panel bracketed pool">
        <div class="panel-hd">
          <span><span class="text-signal/50" aria-hidden="true">▚▚</span> {{ group.label }}</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="panel-body space-y-1.5 font-mono text-sm">
          {% for item in group.items %}
            <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 text-ink-dim">
              <span class="text-signal/40" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>{{ item }}
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ CONTACT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="mb-16" data-reveal>
  {{ rule("channels", "open") }}

  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {% set channels = [
      { label: "github", value: site.github | replace("https://", ""), url: site.github, note: "source & experiments" },
      { label: "mail", value: site.email, url: "mailto:" + site.email, note: "inbox is always open" },
      { label: "rss", value: "/feed.xml", url: "/feed.xml", note: "raw transmission feed" }
    ] %}
    {% for ch in channels %}
      <a href="{{ ch.url }}" {% if ch.label == "github" %}rel="me noopener"{% endif %}
         class="group panel bracketed pool block transition-colors hover:border-signal/50">
        <div class="panel-hd">
          <span><span class="text-signal/50" aria-hidden="true">▚▚</span> {{ ch.label }}</span>
          <span class="text-signal/50 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-body">
          <p class="break-all font-mono text-sm text-ink-hi transition-colors group-hover:text-signal">{{ ch.value }}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">{{ ch.note }}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
